{"absent":["Internal layouts of task, run queue, scheduling class, domain, group and root domain beyond fields named in fragments.","Implementations of domain build, attach, destroy, allocation, capacity scan, housekeeping and architecture topology helpers.","Energy model and frequency control contracts including performance state counts and readiness checks.","Numeric values of realtime ceiling, error codes, domain flags, distance bits and sysctl bounds.","Scheduler invocation, statistics accounting, rescheduling and debugfs update mechanics.","Locking, RCU, cpumask, print, string, capability and error-pointer primitives owned elsewhere.","Cache share computation, effective byte sizing and multi-cache detection details.","NUMA mask construction, nearest-node selection and hop ordering beyond lookup behaviour."],"dossier":"D01","findings":[{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["kernel/sched/syscalls.c::yield_to"],"text":"Cooperative handover from the current donor toward a named task is allowed only inside a shared scheduling class when the class offers the handover hook and the target remains runnable elsewhere; a solitary runnable pair reports absence, a successful handover records statistics and may request remote rescheduling before invoking the scheduler."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["kernel/sched/syscalls.c::sys_sched_get_priority_max","kernel/sched/syscalls.c::sys_sched_get_priority_min"],"text":"Priority range queries separate realtime first-in-first-out and round-robin policies, which expose a positive interval starting at one below the realtime ceiling, from deadline, normal, batch, idle and extensible policies which expose only zero; unknown policies report invalid argument."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["kernel/sched/syscalls.c::sched_rr_get_interval","kernel/sched/syscalls.c::sys_sched_rr_get_interval","kernel/sched/syscalls.c::sys_sched_rr_get_interval_time32"],"text":"Round-robin quantum inquiry resolves a process identifier to its class quantum expressed as a time interval; negative identifiers are invalid, unknown processes are reported missing, permission is checked, and two user layouts serve native and legacy 32-bit callers."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["kernel/sched/syscalls.c::yield_to","kernel/sched/syscalls.c::sched_rr_get_interval","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_update_llc_bytes","kernel/sched/topology.c::partition_sched_domains_locked"],"text":"Target handover holds the target personal lock with interrupts excluded while holding both run queues and retries on migration; quantum inquiry holds read-side protection across lookup plus the target queue lock during class interrogation; cache refresh and partition work hold the domains mutex."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::s_data","kernel/sched/topology.c::s_alloc","kernel/sched/topology.c::__cmp_key"],"text":"Construction context aggregates per-processor shared descriptors, per-processor domain pointers and a root pointer; allocation phases enumerate root, domain, shared, storage and terminator; NUMA search key bundles candidate mask, hop tables, node, position and weight."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_is_eas_possible","kernel/sched/topology.c::build_perf_domains","kernel/sched/topology.c::sysctl_sched_energy_aware","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_energy_present"],"text":"Energy-aware scheduling is considered only when asymmetric capacity markers exist, simultaneous multithreading is inactive, frequency-invariant accounting is present, frequency control is ready, the administrative toggle is enabled and energy model data exists for covered processors."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::build_perf_domains","kernel/sched/topology.c::find_pd","kernel/sched/topology.c::pd_init","kernel/sched/topology.c::destroy_perf_domain_rcu","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_energy_set"],"text":"Performance domain sets move from absent to populated by creating one entry per uncovered processor and publishing under read-side protection, with prior sets reclaimed later; the global energy branch follows whether any surviving set exists, emitting start or stop transitions."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_energy_aware_handler","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_energy_aware_sysctls","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_energy_aware_sysctl_init","kernel/sched/topology.c::rebuild_sched_domains_energy"],"text":"Administrative energy control requires privilege for modification, reports unsupported when the platform cannot satisfy eligibility, otherwise delegates range-checked update and triggers a domain rebuild only on effective change; registration occurs at boot under the kernel namespace."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::default_topology","kernel/sched/topology.c::cpu_smt_flags","kernel/sched/topology.c::tl_smt_mask","kernel/sched/topology.c::cpu_cluster_flags","kernel/sched/topology.c::tl_cls_mask","kernel/sched/topology.c::cpu_core_flags","kernel/sched/topology.c::tl_mc_mask","kernel/sched/topology.c::tl_pkg_mask","kernel/sched/topology.c::cpu_numa_flags","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_numa_mask","kernel/sched/topology.c::arch_llc_mask.alt_1","kernel/sched/topology.c::arch_llc_mask.alt_2"],"text":"Scheduling topology composes threading, cluster, core and package layers with distinct sharing attributes while NUMA layers carry only NUMA marking; cache affinity resolution varies by configuration and package span follows node association."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_numa_find_nth_cpu","kernel/sched/topology.c::hop_cmp","kernel/sched/topology.c::__cmp_key","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_numa_hop_mask"],"text":"NUMA locality queries locate the nth eligible processor within hop-ordered masks, mapping node-less requests to online intersection and node requests to the nearest populated node; hop retrieval validates node and distance bounds and reports busy when tables are absent."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_update_asym_prefer_cpu"],"text":"Asymmetric packing preference tracks the most preferred processor per group, updating when the caller becomes preferred and recomputing by pairwise ranking when its standing degrades; overlapping NUMA copies raise a one-time warning."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::def_root_domain","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_llc","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_llc_size","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_llc_id","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_share_id","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_llc_shared","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_balance_shared","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_numa","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_asym_packing","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_asym_cpucapacity","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_asym_cpucapacity","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_cluster_active","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_cache_present","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_cache_active","kernel/sched/topology.c::sysctl_sched_cache_user","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domain_level_max","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_numa_topology_type","kernel/sched/topology.c::max_lid"],"text":"Core publishes a default root domain, per-processor cache domain pointers with size and identity plus shared and balance hints and NUMA and asymmetry caches, global asymmetry and cluster and cache keys, and tunables for cache use and domain depth."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::destroy_sched_domains_rcu","kernel/sched/topology.c::destroy_perf_domain_rcu","kernel/sched/topology.c::free_asym_cap_entry","kernel/sched/topology.c::detach_destroy_domains"],"text":"Domain chains, performance lists and asymmetry capacity entries retire through deferred reclamation, so read-side observers may briefly see replaced pointers; partition teardown detaches toward the default root while holding appropriate guards."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::TOPOLOGY_SD_FLAGS","kernel/sched/topology.c::NR_DISTANCE_VALUES","kernel/sched/topology.c::SD_FLAG.alt_1","kernel/sched/topology.c::sd_flag_debug","kernel/sched/topology.c::SD_FLAG.alt_2","kernel/sched/topology.c::SD_DEGENERATE_GROUPS_MASK"],"text":"Topology flag aggregate combines capacity sharing, cluster, cache sharing, NUMA and packing aspects; distance table capacity is a power of two derived from bit width; degenerate-group mask and debug names derive from a shared flag list distinguishing group-needing entries."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::partition_sched_domains_locked","kernel/sched/topology.c::dattrs_equal","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domains_mutex","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_energy_mutex","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_energy_update"],"text":"Partition reconstruction assumes the domains mutex is held, evaluates topology changes and capacity scans, reuses identical mask and attribute pairs, records multi-cache presence across reused and new partitions, and serialises energy state changes separately."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::default_relax_domain_level","kernel/sched/topology.c::setup_relax_domain_level","kernel/sched/topology.c::set_sched_topology","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domain_topology","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domain_topology_saved","kernel/sched/topology.c::detach_destroy_domains"],"text":"Relax level defaults to unset and accepts early boot parsing with warning on failure; topology replacement is allowed only before symmetric multiprocessing initialisation completes; teardown decrements asymmetry and cluster keys when previously active."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_update_llc_bytes"],"text":"Cache byte refresh re-evaluates each named processor under mutex using its own cache ancestor to correct early inflated shares and to tolerate departed processors by consulting surviving siblings."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::dattrs_equal","kernel/sched/topology.c::doms_cur","kernel/sched/topology.c::ndoms_cur","kernel/sched/topology.c::dattr_cur","kernel/sched/topology.c::fallback_doms"],"text":"Attribute comparison treats two absent descriptors as equal and otherwise compares against default-initialised content; single-entry fallback and current partition snapshots are retained for reuse detection across rebuilds."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domains_numa_levels","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_numa_node_levels","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_max_numa_distance","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domains_numa_distance","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_numa_node_distance","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domains_numa_masks","kernel/sched/topology.c::numa_node_dist","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_numa_topology_type"],"text":"NUMA distance state comprises level counts, maximum distance, per-level distance tables and hop mask tables, with node distance delegated outward and topology type held globally."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domains_llc_id_allocmask","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domains_tmpmask","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_domains_tmpmask2","kernel/sched/topology.c::sched_debug_setup"],"text":"Temporary domain masks and allocation masks are module-scoped scratch, debug verbosity is enabled through an early boot option, and degenerate domain handling depends on flag metadata rather than inline tests."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/cpumask.h::for_each_cpu"],"text":"Stub for include/linux/cpumask.h::for_each_cpu owned elsewhere."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_1"],"text":"Stub for include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_1 owned elsewhere."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_2"],"text":"Stub for include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_2 owned elsewhere."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_3"],"text":"Stub for include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_3 owned elsewhere."},{"kind":"st